        "text": "Hey Mara,\n\nThank you for putting all of these options together. The direction is definitely moving closer, but I have several notes around colour \\+ scale to make the result softer, more elevated, and more SOLARA COVE.\n\nThe references we provided were intended to evoke something tonal and naturally aged. At present, the artwork feels a little too clean and saturated, so we’d like to bring in additional softness, irregularity, and depth. The aim is for the prints to look collected and textural rather than excessively graphic.\n\nIn general, I think both designs need:\n\\* reduced contrast\n\\* additional grain\n\\* a stronger texture overlay\n\\* edges that are slightly more faded\n\\* less of a “perfect vector” appearance\n\nZebra print:\n\\* The zebra currently appears slightly too yellow/gold and has a little too much contrast.\n\\* I’d like the gold softened into more of a sandy caramel / soft bronze shade.\n\\* Overall, it should look vintage, costly, and sun-faded rather than bright or too golden.\n\\* The bigger, more organic stripe treatment feels like the strongest direction.\n\nWeave print:\n\\* The current weave is leaning somewhat too orange/red.\n\\* I’d like to move it toward a softer brushed brown with greater depth and less warmth.\n\\* Our preferred scale is the larger 5cm diagonal weave, so ideally we would combine:\n→ the tone/colour used in the smaller weave\n→ with the 5cm version’s larger scale.\n\nAcross everything, the result can feel more tonal, softer, and more lived-in—less saturated and polished, and instead more earthy, natural, and collected.\n\nI think we’ll be extremely close once the tones have been refined!"
